# The API is deployed to Render, not Vercel.
#
# vercel.json rewrites every /api/* request to the Render service, so nothing
# here is ever reached on Vercel. Without this file Vercel still auto-detects
# api/ as its serverless-functions directory and compiles api/index.ts on every
# deploy - installing that workspace's dependencies and invoking whatever
# TypeScript version they pin.
#
# That build was always pointless and is now actively harmful:
#
#   1. api/index.ts ends in app.listen() and exports no handler, so the
#      "function" Vercel produced could never have served a request correctly.
#   2. It made the frontend deploy fail on a change to a backend-only
#      dependency - a TypeScript 7 bump broke Vercel's Node builder with
#      "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'readFile')", because the
#      native compiler port no longer exposes the API that builder calls.
#
# Excluding it decouples the two deploys: Render keeps building api/ from this
# same repo (.vercelignore is Vercel-only), and Vercel builds only the SPA.
api
